 <wpt lat="39.71" lon="-105.5819">
  <ele>0.0</ele>
  <time>2024-07-12 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>National Forest outside Crested Butte</name>
  <desc>Free. Beautiful mountain scenery, 15 minutes on dirt road outside town of Crested Butte along Kebler Pass Road. Dirt road but easy to get here in a class C. Kebler Pass Road is a thoroughfare and there&#39;s a lot of traffic on the road.&#xA;&#xA;Gorgeous view to Beckwith Mountain. Easy trail down to the river. There are more campsites at Horse Ranch Park and the Cliff Creek Trailhead just northwest of the GPS marker. Horse Ranch has a pit toilet.&#xA;&#xA;Wildlife includes black bears, elk, beaver, and deer. Mosquitoes were relentless — never camp here without preparation.&#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2024-07-12 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Parking: Yes&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: Yes&#xA;Toilets: No&#xA;Big rig friendly: No&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;Sanitation dump station: No&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/30bcd1a8-08cf-49bd-a3f5-dfa770c5f8a6 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
