 <wpt lat="44.3142" lon="-114.434">
  <ele>0.0</ele>
  <time>2024-07-12 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Near Batty Pass Caves</name>
  <desc>Near the base of Fifty-Mile mountain. Two large, flat, primitive sites can accommodate fairly large groups, plus there is another site farther down with less flat space. This location is very near Batty Pass caves, three old rancher caves worth visiting if you are in the area. This location is also near (on the other side of the Hole-in-the-Rock road) Peek-a-boo and Spooky gulches (part of the upper end of Coyote gulch), two popular, short, and excellent non-technical slot canyons. Dogs are allowed in this location, but note that if you are here for Coyote Gulch features, dogs are not allowed there.&#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2024-07-12 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Parking: Yes&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: No&#xA;Toilets: No&#xA;Big rig friendly: No&#xA;Tent friendly: Yes&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;Sanitation dump station: No&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/f8fc7603-5d0d-40a4-b814-3303b1232f5e (network required)&#xA;</desc>
