 <wpt lat="34.5691" lon="-105.8085">
  <ele>0.0</ele>
  <time>2024-07-12 00:00:00 UTC</time>
  <name>Trinidad Rest Area Southbound</name>
  <desc>There is a sign that posts an 8 hour limit. Plenty of car spots and truck spots as well. The rest area has running water, trash cans, picnic tables and flush toilets (heated bathrooms which is a plus). Another nice thing to find out, is that you can use stoves (either at the picnic tables, or outside of your vehicle). They are patrolled by both state troopers and highway patrol and I would think are pretty safe.&#xA;Starlink is 200 mbps down. I arrived at 9 pm. A couple of rvs and trucks. TMobile and Verizon are not working. No rv dump.&#xA;&#xA;Date verified: 2024-07-12 00:00:00 UTC&#xA;Open: Yes&#xA;Electricity: No&#xA;Wifi: No&#xA;Kitchen: No&#xA;Parking: Yes&#xA;Restaurant: No&#xA;Showers: No&#xA;Water: Yes&#xA;Toilets: Yes&#xA;Big rig friendly: Yes&#xA;Tent friendly: No&#xA;Pet friendly: Yes&#xA;Sanitation dump station: No&#xA;&#xA;https://ioverlander.com/places/c39ce950-1c8c-4321-a7e9-0f21754b1e73 (network required)&#xA;</desc>
  <type>Informal Campsite</type>
  <extensions>
